{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.route_c_m2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.route_c_m2","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AomegaM2BPSCohomology.lean#L110-L120","doc":"**Route C M2 (closed-sector BPS cohomology check).** The certified eq-(98)\ndatum yields: chirality spectrum `{3,4}` (`4` in `S⁺`, `3` in `S⁻`), bar split\n`(7,1)`, `4₁` dimension `s(1)=3`, `5₂` extra state `s(1)+1`, and (the structural\npoint) pairwise-distinct Borel rays — so the Davison–Meinhardt spectrum is abelian\nand `dim BPS = |Ω|` exactly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.fivetwo_extra_state","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.fivetwo_extra_state","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AomegaM2BPSCohomology.lean#L103-L106","doc":"**The `5₂` `S⁺` count is `s(1) + 1`**, and (rays distinct) the `+1` is a genuine\nextra BPS state at a distinct Borel ray, not a motivic multiplicity on a repeated\ncharge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.fourone_dim_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.fourone_dim_three","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AomegaM2BPSCohomology.lean#L99-L101","doc":"**`dim H_BPS(4₁) = s(1) = 3 = A_ω(4₁)`**: three unit-multiplicity BPS states,\none per meridian charge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.sAtOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.sAtOne","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AomegaM2BPSCohomology.lean#L96-L97","doc":"`s(1)` = total dimension of the `4₁` meridian-charge BPS cohomology. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.sMultiplicities","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.sMultiplicities","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AomegaM2BPSCohomology.lean#L91-L94","doc":"The `4₁` meridian-charge polynomial `s(x) = x + 1 + x⁻¹` (GGM eq 188), as the\nmultiplicities of the three unit-degeneracy generators graded by meridian charge\n`e ∈ {−1, 0, +1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.bar_split_seven_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.bar_split_seven_one","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AomegaM2BPSCohomology.lean#L85-L87","doc":"**The bar-eigenspace split of the `{3,4}` chirality pair is `(7,1)`** (M0's\ngrading, recovered on the reconstructed BPS dimensions). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.barOdd","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AomegaM2BPSCohomology.lean#L82-L83","doc":"Bar-odd component of `(4,3)`: `4 − 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.barEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.barEven","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AomegaM2BPSCohomology.lean#L79-L80","doc":"Bar-even component of `(4,3)`: `4 + 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.bps_spectrum_three_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.bps_spectrum_three_four","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AomegaM2BPSCohomology.lean#L70-L75","doc":"**The chirality-graded BPS spectrum is `{3, 4}`** — `dim = 4` in `S⁺`,\n`dim = 3` in `S⁻`, and they differ. With the rays distinct (above), Davison–\nMeinhardt gives `dim BPS = |Ω|` with no q-correction, so these integers are the\nfull BPS-cohomology dimensions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.dimBPSminus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.dimBPSminus","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AomegaM2BPSCohomology.lean#L67-L68","doc":"`dim H_BPS` at the distinguished `S⁻` ray = `|Ω(σ₀,σ₂)|`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.dimBPSplus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.dimBPSplus","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AomegaM2BPSCohomology.lean#L64-L65","doc":"`dim H_BPS` at the distinguished `S⁺` ray = the eq-(98) constant `|Ω(σ₀,σ₁)|`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.sminus_rays_nodup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.sminus_rays_nodup","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AomegaM2BPSCohomology.lean#L59-L60","doc":"**The `S⁻` Borel rays are pairwise distinct.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.splus_rays_nodup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.splus_rays_nodup","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AomegaM2BPSCohomology.lean#L54-L57","doc":"**The `S⁺` Borel rays are pairwise distinct.** No two BPS states of this\nchirality share a charge — the hypothesis that makes the Davison–Meinhardt\nplethystic log trivial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.sminusRays","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.sminusRays","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AomegaM2BPSCohomology.lean#L51-L52","doc":"The Borel rays of the `S⁻(0)` spectrum generator (eq-(97) order). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.splusRays","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology.splusRays","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AomegaM2BPSCohomology.lean#L47-L49","doc":"The Borel rays (factor positions) of the `S⁺(0)` spectrum generator, in the\neq-(96) order `S_{σ₃σ₁}·S_{σ₃σ₂}·S_{σ₁σ₂}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}